## history
### 2026-10-17 (UTC) — the unlanded friendrows area opens every bound a code path does not enforce
- baseline created over 21 tables — data written BEFORE this point is not covered by it

### 2026-10-17 (UTC) — FriendStatus.status becomes open text: FriendRows shows any word outside FriendStates as down and accepts any length
- FriendStatus.status: wire kind 12 -> 17 [refuse]
- FriendStatus.status: nested table string added [refuse]

### 2026-10-17 (UTC) — a8-strangers-writer: Stranger table
- no compatibility-affecting edits; the wire absorbs the rest

### 2026-10-17 (UTC) — Stranger is a server-owned record, so by S1 it is a fixed table, not a variable one: seen becomes Unix nanoseconds UTC int64
- Stranger.seen: wire kind 17 -> 5 [refuse]
- Stranger.seen: nested table string removed — the field keeps its wire kind, so no reader can report the change (docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §4) [refuse]
